"""SK-12D29-G060 - SPDT right-angle slide switch, 6.0 mm lever, through hole. Bare part.

Datasheet: G-Switch drawing SK-12D29-GXXX, 2016-05-29 (one page), LCSC C2848877.

Ratings ("G-Switch Specification"): DC 24 V 1.0 A; contact resistance 50 mOhm max; insulation
resistance 100 MOhm min at DC 250 V; withstand AC 250 V for 1 min; -25 to +70 C; life 10,000
cycles.

Mechanics (drawing): body 8.6 x 3.6 mm (top view) and 3.6 mm high (side view); lever SQ1.5
(1.5 x 1.5 mm), length G = 6.0 mm for G060 (switch height table), 2 mm travel; black lever (LCSC
listing). Three pins at 2.0 mm pitch and two frame legs 8.3 mm apart, all on one line (P.C.B
LAYOUT, bottom view), 0.3 mm thick; the pins leave the body 0.8 mm from its rear face (the face
opposite the lever) and stand about 2.2 mm proud of the body (side view, 5.8 - 3.6 mm), so the
lever lies parallel to the board.

Pins (SCHEMATIC, non-shorting): the centre pin (2) is the common; the slider joins it to the
outer pin on one side or the other. The symbol names them A (pin 1) and B (pin 3), as the
MK-12D18 package does. TODO: the drawing does not say which lever position joins which outer pin;
check on a sample before the silkscreen marks ON.

Footprint: the drawing does not dimension the holes. Scaled from it against its 2 mm pitch: about
0.8 mm for the pins and 1.1 mm for the frame legs, which take the 0.3 mm thick pins and legs. The
legs are unnumbered plated pads (mechanical, no net).
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Current", "Voltage")

COM = io(Net)
A = io(Net)
B = io(Net)

# G-Switch Specification: DC 24 V 1.0 A.
voltage = Voltage("24V")
current = Current("1A")

Component(
    name="SK-12D29-G060",
    prefix="SW",
    symbol=Symbol(library="SK-12D29-G060.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("SW-TH_SK-12D29-G060.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="SK-12D29-G060", manufacturer="G-Switch"),
    pins={
        "A": A,
        "COM": COM,
        "B": B,
    },
    properties={
        "voltage": voltage,
        "current": current,
    },
)
